"""pktrec-web - web interface of the FPGA Packet Recorder.

A small HTTP server (Python 3 standard library only) that serves a single-page
UI and a JSON API on the board's PS Ethernet port. It drives the existing
command-line tools as subprocesses:

  pktrec-phy status --json / path port link state, per-pair TAP/monitor mode
  pktrec-cap stats --json         capture block counters (per port), timebase
  pktrec-cap record --stats-json  one capture at a time, to <rec-dir>/captures;
                                  live statistics as JSON lines on its stdout
  pktrec-cap info                 capture file header (text, for the info view)
  pktrec-export <file> -o -       streamed to the browser as pcapng (no temp file)
  /run/pktrec/tb.json             timebase discipline state (pktrec-tb daemon)
  /etc/pktrec/calibration.conf    calibration file (+ /run/pktrec/calibration.json:
                                  applied at boot by pktrec-calibration.service)

(The text outputs of pktrec-phy status / pktrec-cap stats are still parsed as a
fallback when a tool does not know --json.)

There is no authentication: run it on a trusted network only.

API (all JSON, errors as {"error": "..."} with an HTTP status code):
  GET    /api/status                 ports, pair modes, capture, disk, time (with the
                                     timebase discipline), calibration, versions
  GET    /api/stats                  live counters and rates (poll every second)
  POST   /api/mode                   {"pair": 0|1, "mode": "tap"|"monitor"}
  POST   /api/capture/start          {"ports": [0..3], "snaplen": N, "duration_s": S,
                                      "size_bytes": B, "name": "..."}
  POST   /api/capture/stop
  GET    /api/captures               list of capture files (from their 4 KB headers)
  GET    /api/captures/<name>/info   header fields + 'pktrec-cap info' text
  GET    /api/captures/<name>.pcapng download, converted on the fly by pktrec-export
  GET    /api/captures/<name>.cap    download the raw capture file
  DELETE /api/captures/<name>        delete a capture

--mock replaces the tools by sw/pktrec-web/mock_tools.py (host testing, no board).
"""

